//~ compile_fail(backend)
//~ error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch

// NEGATIVE (must FAIL to compile): send Tattach before Tversion.
//
// `attach` accepts only <!negotiated>, and the only tor that mints it is
// `reply.release`, reachable only through `version`. So the first message on a
// 9P connection is Tversion or the program does not compile.
//
// THIS RULE HAS NO ASSERTION AND NO BRANCH ANYWHERE IN `uk9p`. It is the 9P2000
// protocol's rule, not Unikraft's — "the first message on a connection must be
// Tversion", because Tversion both settles the message size and RESETS the
// connection, invalidating every outstanding fid and tag. `lib/uk9p` has no
// opinion about it: `uk_9p_attach` (9p.c:144) builds a Tattach out of whatever
// state the device is in and sends it.
//
// And the device LOOKS ready, which is what makes this worth a compile error
// rather than a comment. `uk_9pdev_connect` sets `dev->msize = dev->max_msize`
// (9pdev.c:247) precisely so that an un-versioned device has a usable message
// size, so nothing downstream reads as uninitialized. Against QEMU the Tattach
// is answered with an Rerror and the program gets an errno from a round trip.
// Against a lenient server it is answered normally, and the connection runs at
// a message size the two ends never agreed on — the failure is then a truncated
// read, later, on a large file.
//
// This is the `unikraft/vmem` shape: a real ordering rule whose penalty is not
// a check. Lifting it costs one phantom state.
//
// EXPECTED: error[KORU030]: Phantom state mismatch: expected
//           'unikraft.ninep:negotiated' but got 'unikraft.ninep:linked!'
//           for argument 'dev'

// The `unikraft` namespace is declared here, not inherited: koruc's built-in
// alias probes the sibling koru-libs CHECKOUT, so in a worktree this file would
// otherwise compile against main's lifts instead of the ones beside it.
~std/compiler:paths {
    unikraft: {{ ENTRY }}/../..
}

~import unikraft/ninep
~import std/io

~unikraft/ninep:connect(tag: "korufs")
| ok mount |> unikraft/ninep:attach(dev: mount, uname: "korunaut", aname: "")
    | ok tree |> std/io:print.ln("should never get here")
        |> unikraft/ninep:walk.skipped(root: tree): spent
            |> unikraft/ninep:session.end(root: spent)
                | ok ended |> unikraft/ninep:disconnect(ended.dev)
    | refused e |> std/io:print.ln("attach: {{ e.reason:s }}")
        |> unikraft/ninep:session.skipped(e.dev): unused
            |> unikraft/ninep:disconnect(dev: unused)
| absent why |> std/io:print.ln("connect: {{ why:s }}")
| refused e |> std/io:print.ln("connect: {{ e.reason:s }}")
